  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Calculate, in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{11}{13}$ for $-{180}^{\u2218}<x\\le {180}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{11}{13})=-57.795\\,772{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248-{57.796}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{57.796}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{57.796}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={57.796}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={57.796}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/f204faa6327d057dbea5de66f2c6ffca0a9982c299d1e4278dbc6514ddf016df.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{57.796}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={237.796}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=X-{360}^{\u2218}={237.796}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218}=-{122.204}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x=-{122}^{\u2218},-{58}^{\u2218}.$",
